{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510516-whom-would-you-cast-as-the-antidulivans","id":1510516,"title":"Whom would you cast as the Antidulivans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-02T12:40:58-07:00","id":1510516,"title":"Whom would you cast as the Antidulivans?","content":"Just a fun idea to play with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T16:02:31-07:00","id":1510526,"title":"","content":"For the Tzimisce antediluvian i've used Bela Lugosi, because the name means &quot;Bela of Lugoj&quot;, James Earl Jones' Thulsa Doom for Set and De Niro's Travis Bickle in Taxi Driver for Kapaneus/Ankla Hotep.<br /> Guess i'm a low hanging fruit kind of ST. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-02-2023, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T16:45:47-07:00","id":1510530,"title":"","content":"Jim Carrey would make a perfect Malkav. Brendan Fraser could pull of the male brujah anti who was said to have been diablarised by one of his childer. Tremere could be played by Keanue Reeves, he's already done something similar when he was Jhon Constantine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T23:15:36-07:00","id":1510567,"title":"","content":"<b>Veddartha</b> - Bill Nighy<br /> <b>Arikel</b>, the Sculptor - Melanie Iglesias<br /> <b>Ishtar,</b> the bull-dancer - Sunny Leone<br /> <b>Sargon </b>- Christopher Lee (in his Saruman outfit; with heavy makeup/CGI to raflect the curse of the Clan of Death death-like appearance)<br /> <b>Ilyes </b>- Dolph Lundgren (from the eighties)<br /> <b>Troile </b>- Milla Jovovich<br /> <b>Absimiliard </b>- Danny de vito (like how he was the Pinguin, mr. de Vito is the master of disguise) in heavy makeup/CGI after-transformation; before transformation/Obfuscated form Arnold Schwarzenegger from the Predator era)<br /> <b>Laza Omri Baras</b> - Kevin Sorbo (with two shadow panther and CGI)<br /> <b>Ennoia</b> - Linda Hamilton (from Terminator 2: Judgment Day)<br /> <b>Zapathasura</b> - Kartik Aaryan<br /> <b>Haqim </b>- Omar Sharif (from his late years to captrue Haqim scholar/wise old warrior aspect)<br /> <b>Malkav </b>- David Tennant (as the twin brother of Arikel and Malakai this one was hard; <b>Malakai</b> would be Georgia Moffett of course)<br /> <b>Saulot</b> - Chris Evans<br /> <b>The Eldest </b>- William Hartnell (or David Bradley who chanelled his inner Hartnell marvelously)<br /> <b>Sutekh </b>- Dwayne &quot;the Rock&quot; Johnson<br /> <b>Tremere </b>- Robert Downey jr<br /> <b>Augustus Giovanni </b>- Roberto Benigni<br /> <br /> <b>Lilith</b> - Sigourney weaver<br /> <b>Caine</b> - Ricardo Montalb\u00e1n<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T23:32:37-07:00","id":1510569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Saulot</b> - Chris Evans\u200b </div> </div> </div>Damn! Now I'll never be able to remove from my head the image of sexy shirtless Chris Evans (as Captain America) as Saulot... hahaha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T00:10:03-07:00","id":1510572,"title":"","content":"Well Saulot reminded Cain of Abel, and Chris Evans fit that role (especially if Ricardo Montalb\u00e1n is Caine... KHAAAAAAAN - sorry, had to)<br /> Saulot was also known as Zao-Lat, Zao, the Dragon, or the Warlord, he was gentle,. serene, righteous, but strong, fierce enemy of the Baali - so was a bit like Captian America <br /> And while experimented following the Howl of the Devil Tiger Dharma, managed to make the Baali - and a &quot;dark&quot; Chris Evans is awesome picture <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T09:12:05-07:00","id":1510607,"title":"","content":"Tzismce: Billy Drago as he made a career playing eerie inhuman seeming people from Frank Nitti in The Untouchables, Fench In Cyborg 2 and the Demon of Fear in Charmed. I can't think of to many actors who could pull it off in recent memory. Alas he died a few years back and I don't know who could play the Eldest now<br /> <br /> Brujah/Troile: I'd choose Collin Ferrel as the rebel who diablerized his sire and got cursed with the temper.<br /> <br /> Malkav: Johnny Depp has played off kilter roles in the past and was known for it before he got tapped to play Captain Jack Sparrow.<br /> <br /> Set: This is a hard one as Set is one of my favorite mythological figures and I considered Dave Baustia for the role because of sheer physical presence and willingness to try out new roles.<br /> <br /> Tremere: Hey Keanu Reeves played mystics like John Constatine and Neo before and this would be a easy role to slip into. Before that it would have been Peter Cushing.<br /> <br /> Cappadicous: Christian Bale can play any role as he showed in Batman, Thor and numerous other.<br /> <br /> Gangrel: Milo Jovich of course as she made a career playing survivlists.<br /> <br /> The Original Brujah: I would cast a much younger Sir Christopher Lee in the role as he could embody the cold, emotionless and scholary side of the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-03-2023, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T13:25:02-07:00","id":1510630,"title":"","content":"Julian Sands I might cast as Augustus Giovanni as he gives a good cold blooded calculating vibe as the former head of the clan. But alas he is still missing and presumed dead in the Mount Shasta region. So I might cast Hugh Laurie instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T13:36:22-07:00","id":1510631,"title":"","content":"All of them: Obvious Nicholas Cage CGI face-swaps onto body doubles. It's the closest we can get to approximating the mind blowing insanity of the ancient blood-gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T14:06:53-07:00","id":1510637,"title":"","content":"<br /> Set:: Peter Williams (Apophis in Stargate SG 1) or Arnold Vosloo (the mummy)<br /> Tzimisce Antediluvian: David Palffy (Sokar in Stargate SG 1).<br /> Cappadocius: Mark Harelik (God in Preacher).<br /> Absimilliard: Bill Skarsgard in make up!<br /> Troile: Melina Juergens (from hellblade)<br /> Haqim: Ghassan Massoud in make up! (Saladin kingdom of heaven)<br /> Arikel: the late Aaliyah would have been great!<br /> <br /> Cain: Timothy Omundson!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 05-03-2023, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T15:05:49-07:00","id":1510643,"title":"","content":"I would use models rather than actors, because I don't want them to seem familiar, and their speaking rolls will be light because they're mysterious. Also, because a story more likely to use -This is what character A imagines happened in a past he's not quite privy too- rather than actually swing out an ante, you're free to change model for different character perspective. Particularly useful with characters like [Brujah] where there's a good chunk of debate. (More likely to use Augustus,Capadocious,Tremere or Lasombra. Could use Tzmisce but, y'know... Tzmisce) <br /> <br /> <br /> Set: Red headed bodybuilder. <br /> Asmilibard: African<br /> Haqim: Middle eastern features but skin is 0*0*0 levels of dark. <br /> Giovanni/Tremere: let's make them blond and blue eyed to be distinct. <br /> Basically everyone else: Brown eyes, brown or black hair, pale vampiric skin. Mostly west asia/north african features. <br /> <br /> I think I'd make Triole a black man. Enoia could be anything. <br /> <br /> I'm on the fence on whether or not Antideluvians should exhibit their curses or not, since my theory is that while most vampires think the antideluvians were cursed for their behaviours in actuality they deliberately gave those curses to their childer for social cohesion and it doesn't apply to them unless they will it. They've all probably mastered obfuscate too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T09:17:16-07:00","id":1510706,"title":"","content":"I've always imagined Augustus Giovanni as William Hickey based on his role in <i>Prizzi's Honor\u200b</i>.<br /> <br /> The only antediluvian where a modern, available casting choice cries out to me is John Noble as the Tzimisce antediluvian if it decides to manifest in a human shape. It would most likely be represented by practical effects of the John Carpenter's <i>The Thing</i> variety rather than a particular actor, though.<br /> <br /> I'd pick Kathleen Turner to voice Ennoia, but she'd be animated landscape, not a human figure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T14:55:49-07:00","id":1510721,"title":"","content":"I imagine them that way for some reason:<br /> <br /> Brujah: African or Afro-descendant appearing to be close to 40, but with a well defined body.<br /> <br /> Troile: Same as Brujah, just a little younger, between 26 and 29 years old, enough for you to assume it was his son.<br /> <br /> Ventrue: Either a white man with short black hair and a beard cut to size, or of Indian descent but with harder features.<br /> <br /> Ennoia: African or Afro-descendant, short stature, well-built body, messy curly hair, prefers road or practical clothes, looks don't matter. Eyes of an intense yellow resembling those of a large feline.<br /> <br /> Toreador: Individual of indeterminate gender, short average height, blood red hair, no sign of a beard, large lips, light eyes, ivory-white skin, sweet and slightly raspy voice usually associated with women, but can be male tooo, no sign of body hair or sharp curves.<br /> <br /> Absimiliard: Bluish skin, pointy chin, body covered with tumors of various sizes, long fingernails, large and pointed ears that resemble those of a bat.<br /> <br /> Goratrix: For some reason I think of him as a man with tanned skin, excessively long beard and hair, and brown eyes.<br /> <br /> Malkav: Albino male, excessively thin, messy white hair, large clear eyes covered by a black circle typical of people with insomnia for some time, uncomfortable look.<br /> <br /> Ravnos: Woman with long hair... that's all.<br /> <br /> Lasombra: European woman of tall stature, sharp nose, wide forehead, thin neck, long black hair.<br /> <br /> Tzimice: I imagine he doesn't have a human form, but if he did it would be something more bestial, like a Garou in Glabro form.<br /> <br /> Set: Tall male, dark or tanned skin, defined physique, no hair other than eyebrows, snake tattoos on different body parts.<br /> <br /> Haqim: I'm thinking of someone of middle eastern descent, well-trained physique, but compact so as not to impair mobility or stealth.<br /> <br /> Cappadocian: An elderly gentleman, 70 years or older.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T09:27:49-07:00","id":1510889,"title":"","content":"Nicolas Cage would make a great Malkav along with Johnny Depp. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T10:26:58-07:00","id":1510893,"title":"","content":"Nicolas Cage would be very cartoonish in this role, so I don't know, Johnny Depp even has a mannerism, but I don't think he would be good, at most a functional villain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T11:25:39-07:00","id":1510898,"title":"","content":"I think Cage can dial it back and he has shown that he can serious roles in the past and Depp would be interesting in the role. I'm still having trouble who could play Lasombra perfectly. I'd think Idris Elba would perfect in the role and then I thought more and more that he would make a way better Montano then the antidulivan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-06-2023, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T14:15:19-07:00","id":1510914,"title":"","content":"While my first post was a bit silly, I'm actually a bit serious too. I don't view the Antedeluvians as some staid beings that should be hanging around being serious dramatic figures. I want them to have that bombastic off-kilter thing that Cage is famous for because we're talking about beings thousands of years old, with powers so vast that the idea that even the most dedicated of them to it are still so detached from humanity that passing as &quot;normal&quot; just isn't possible for long. While I love so many of the actors people have thought of, the problem is that they'll end up humanizing these beings too much. <br /> <br /> Nick Cage has an unpredictable energy that really do think - with the right team working with him - would be unparalleled for communicated what it's like being a in a room with one of these creatures. While a lot of his performances have been memed to death and all, take something like the alphabet scene from Vampire's Kiss. That sudden manic rant that could be nothing, or could turn into a psychotic snap, and is the kind of vibe being around the Antes should be like. You should never know if they're just expressing themselves oddly because they're so inhuman and it's nothing, or if some ghoul's fuck up is turning into a simmering Frenzy with their kind of power about to go off unchecked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T10:17:40-07:00","id":1510990,"title":"","content":"Nicolas Cage really put his teeth into the Dracula role in Renfield. I\u2019m sorry I couldn\u2019t resist the pun there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T14:33:05-07:00","id":1511020,"title":"","content":"It's the first thing I've seen him do in years where he wasn't phoning it in. (Disclaimer: I have not yet seen Mandy.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T09:19:06-07:00","id":1511543,"title":"","content":"You got to give Nic Cage credit at that his work ethic is solid despite the somewhat low budget films he has been in recent years and even his crappy films he was in he still put in the effort to put in good work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}